From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t31: clear a stale sensor proc tree on init

If a previous tx-isp instance left /proc/jz/sensor behind, the next
module init recreates the directory and its files over the stale ones,
and procfs warns about duplicate entries. Remove the old subtree before
creating the fresh one.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
+++ b/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
@@ -1482,8 +1482,11 @@
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 17, 0)
 	/* Mainline procfs no longer accepts a slash in a single entry name. */
 	tx_isp_sinfo_jz_root = tx_isp_get_jz_proc_root();
-	if (tx_isp_sinfo_jz_root)
+	if (tx_isp_sinfo_jz_root) {
+		/* A previous tx-isp instance may have left the tree behind. */
+		remove_proc_subtree("sensor", tx_isp_sinfo_jz_root);
 		tx_isp_sinfo_root = proc_mkdir("sensor", tx_isp_sinfo_jz_root);
+	}
 #else
 	tx_isp_sinfo_root = proc_mkdir("jz/sensor", NULL);
 #endif
